      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T11:18:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We originally thought about changing the API surface. After talking to Gavin, we decided to go with the header for a couple of reasons:\n\n- The current parameters branch \u0026 target identify which manifest to return. implicit/explicit is client invocation metadaata and tells why the call is happening which seemed like the wrong type of data to send over for this endpoint similar to User-Agent.\n\n- Header also allows to pass over this info while being backward compatible without changing public protocol. XML-RPC only supports positional arguments and does not marshal None by default since it\u0027s initialized with \"allow_none\u003dFalse\", which means the client cannot call `GetApprovedManifest(branch, None, mode)` which would lead to errors. `GetApprovedManifest(branch, mode)` would collide with target.\n\n- The behavior of the API stays the same regardless of what type of call this is. The server returns (ok, manifest_xml) which repo uses to sync. Or False when unavailable, which implicit sync treats as a ToT fallback on our server.\n\nHappy to chat about this further if you feel this isn\u0027t the right direction.",
      "parentUuid": "c272053c_7eef0635",
      "revId": "ce25e9410e5ee0a699c7063dc9fa8996b746cb02",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
